  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Lincoln returns six weeks after starting sertraline 50 mg daily for a moderate depressive episode. His mood is brighter on most days, and he is enjoying his work again. He is back at court on his usual schedule and writes letters to friends two or three times a week. He falls asleep within half an hour and wakes once a night, compared with the broken sleep he described at intake, and his concentration on long briefs is better. Mild nausea in the first two weeks settled by the third week. He has had no headache, diarrhea, restlessness, or sexual side effects. He misses about one dose every two weeks. He has had no suicidal thoughts since the intake visit and still carries his safety plan. He drinks no alcohol. He saw Dr. Natarajan of psychiatry this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Mood brighter on most days; back to court work and letters to friends</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Asleep within half an hour; wakes once a night</td></tr><tr><td>Medication tolerance</td><td>Nausea resolved by week three; no other adverse effects</td></tr><tr><td>Adherence</td><td>Misses about one dose every two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts since intake; safety plan carried</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>9, down from 14</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

